[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 1. **Public entry points (4).** `nm -D` and `grep -nE '^void' c_src/src/driver.c`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    agree on the full set. `include/driver.h` only declares `driver`, the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    *convenience / one-shot wrapper*; the three lower-level entry points
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    (`printIntPtrLine`, `good`, `bad`) are non-`static` and therefore part of the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    public ABI and must be driven **directly**, not only through `driver`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    Call hierarchy: `driver` → {`good`, `bad`} → `printIntPtrLine` → `printf`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 2. **Runtime options/flags: exactly one.** `driver(int useGood)`, tested by the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    single `if (useGood)` at `driver.c:50`. State it toggles: which of the two
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    lower-level entry points runs. Two states: zero and non-zero. There are no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    other options, no global config, no init function, no `#ifdef` (grep for
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `#if` finds only the `DRIVER_H_` include guard), and Cargo.toml declares no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `[features]`, so there is exactly **one** feature combination to verify.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 3. **Input shapes for `printIntPtrLine`'s `const int *`:**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    * *value* shape, because the sink is `printf("%d")`: `0`, `+1`, `-1`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m      `INT_MAX`, `INT_MIN`, random 32-bit patterns.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    * *pointer provenance* shape: stack, heap, static/`.data`, aligned vs
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m      misaligned. The C does an unaligned-tolerant `mov (%rax),%eax`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 4. **Call-sequence / stack-state shape.** This is a real axis rather than an
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    invented one: `bad` reads an *uninitialized stack slot*, so its output is a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    function of what previous calls left on the stack. The composed pipeline is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    therefore observable, and per-wrapper tests cannot see it. Distinct shapes:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    nothing-before, `good` before, `printIntPtrLine` before, `driver(1)` before,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `bad` twice, and reached-via-`driver` (which inserts one extra stack frame)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    versus called-directly.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 5. **Output-stream shape.** `printf` is the only side effect, so stdout
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    buffering mode is part of the observable surface: pipe (fully buffered) vs
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    line buffered, and byte-exact ordering across many calls in one process.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
